Task: Add migration V6 + OrderStore.updateStatusIfCurrent + tests (US-6.3 Phase 1)

Summary: Added V6__add_payment_status_values.sql (drop+recreate
order_status_check to include 'confirmed'/'payment_failed' alongside the
existing three values). Added a new atomic guarded-transition method,
updateStatusIfCurrent(id, expected, newStatus), to the OrderStore trait and
both impls - keyed directly by order id (unlike updateStatusByItemId, which
joins through order_items), since payment.settled/payment.failed events
carry orderId, not an item id. Only transitions if the order's current
status equals expected; returns None (idempotent no-op) otherwise, or for
an unknown/malformed id. In-memory impl uses Ref.modify's atomic
compare-and-swap; Postgres impl adds a new prepared query
(updateOrderStatusIfCurrent) with WHERE id = ? AND status = ?, mirroring
updateOrderStatusByItemId's RETURNING shape.

Also fixed 3 pre-existing test-double OrderStore[IO] implementations
(HealthRoutesSuite x2, OrderRoutesSuite x2) that needed the new trait method
added to compile - found immediately via the compiler, not missed.

Files changed:
- src/main/resources/db/migration/V6__add_payment_status_values.sql (new)
- src/main/scala/orderservice/OrderStore.scala
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderStoreSuite.scala
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderStorePostgresSuite.scala
- src/test/scala/orderservice/HealthRoutesSuite.scala
- src/test/scala/orderservice/OrderRoutesSuite.scala
- several other test files reformatted by scalafmt incidentally (pre-existing
  line-length violations from US-5.4's 4th constructor param, unrelated to
  this task's logic - confirmed whitespace-only via git diff before bundling)

Verification: 125/125 tests pass (62 non-Postgres + 30 Postgres/Testcontainers
+ others), including 30/30 in OrderStorePostgresSuite proving the migration
applies cleanly (schema version 6) and the new method's 3 behaviors (success,
wrong-current-status no-op, unknown-id no-op) against real Postgres.

Why: payment.settled/payment.failed consumer (Phase 2) needs an atomic,
race-free way to transition an order from Reserved to Confirmed/PaymentFailed
by orderId, without regressing a later/terminal status on a redelivered or
out-of-order event.
